  "$comment": "Subject -> category for graph consumers. Order IS the display sequence. Seeded 2026-08-20 from a 13-scout extraction over a 285-context recruiting platform. Categories follow the chronology of a hire (define the role -> source -> read the evidence -> assess -> decide -> operate the pipeline -> treat the candidate well) with two cross-cutting rings (governance, measurement). One bundle on purpose: every category shares the recruiting purity denylist, so no split is earned yet (see knowledge/README.md). Leads recorded but NOT forged, with their demand evidence, so a later pass can reconsider rather than re-derive: (1) role-automatability-assessment - a per-responsibility automatable/assisted/human-only taxonomy plus a complete|temporary|unassessed fit verdict, found outside every scout territory; a genuine theory of which parts of a role must stay human, folded out only because it sits at the edge of hiring and job design. (2) hiring-workspace-readiness - what a talent team must configure before it can hire; thin, and mostly product onboarding. (3) recruiting-authority-and-need-to-know - proposed by two scouts and then FALSIFIED by a third: the seat taxonomy does not encode candidate-visibility boundaries (recruiter and hiring-manager hold identical capabilities), so need-to-know is governed by consent and tenancy, not by role. Do not forge it without new evidence.",
